---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Quick"
  description="Privacy Policy for Quick covering UK GDPR rights, personal data processing, retention, and contact details."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="How Quick collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information in line with UK GDPR requirements."
    imageSrc="/images/copertina.webp"
    imageAlt="Privacy and data protection policy"
  />

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container stack">
      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 13 March 2026</p>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how Quick ("we", "us", "our") processes personal data when you visit
          `paywithquick.co.uk`, contact us, or use our merchant services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
        <p>
          Quick is the data controller for personal data collected through this website.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contact: <a href="mailto:info@paywithquick.co.uk">info@paywithquick.co.uk</a><br />
          Address: Ingeborg, Middle Hill, Egham, England, TW20 0JG
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>2. Personal data we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Contact details you submit (for example name, email address, message content).</li>
          <li>Technical data such as browser type, IP address, and device information.</li>
          <li>Cookie consent choices and limited analytics data where consent is provided.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>3. How and why we use your data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Respond to enquiries and provide requested information.</li>
          <li>Operate, maintain, and secure our website and services.</li>
          <li>Monitor performance and improve user experience (for consented analytics).</li>
          <li>Meet legal, regulatory, and compliance obligations.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>4. UK GDPR lawful bases</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> website security, service improvement, fraud prevention.</li>
          <li><strong>Consent:</strong> optional cookies/analytics and similar technologies.</li>
          <li><strong>Contract / pre-contract:</strong> when handling merchant onboarding or service requests.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> where processing is required by law or regulation.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>5. Sharing data</h2>
        <p>
          We may share data with trusted service providers that support hosting, website delivery, and operational tooling.
          We require appropriate safeguards and contractual protections.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
        <p>
          If personal data is transferred outside the UK, we implement appropriate safeguards such as adequacy decisions
          or approved contractual protections.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including legal,
          accounting, and compliance requirements.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK GDPR, you may have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access your personal data.</li>
          <li>Request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
          <li>Request deletion (where applicable).</li>
          <li>Restrict or object to processing.</li>
          <li>Request data portability (where applicable).</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent where processing relies on consent.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="surface-card feature-card">
        <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you have concerns about how we handle personal data, contact us first at
          <a href="mailto:info@paywithquick.co.uk">info@paywithquick.co.uk</a>.
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO):
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
